; STAR-Writer — basic STELLAR text-entry terminal
; Loads at $4000 (VM1 program block).
; Text buffer: $0A00..$0FFF relative  ( = $4A00..$4FFF absolute ).
; MEMMODE left at default 1 (Relative).
;
; Keys:  CR       = store CR+LF, echo CR+LF
;        BS ($08) = backspace - drop last char (drops 2 for CR+LF pair),
;                   echo BS SP BS
;        ^D ($04) = silent delete (drops 2 for CR+LF pair)
;        ^E ($05) = end - scan buffer for $00 sentinel, set R1 there,
;                   replay the loaded text, ready to continue typing
;        ^U ($15) = clear - zero the whole buffer, reset pointer, CR+LF
;        ^V ($16) = view - dump buffer to terminal
;        ^X ($18) = exit - write $00 sentinel at M(R1), HALT (text stays)
;
; Init does NOT clear buffer memory — only loads vCPU register state.
; ^X writes a $00 byte after the last typed char so that ^E on a later
; run can find where the text ends.  On a fresh cold boot ^E will
; typically see $00 at $4A00 and act as empty.
;
; vCPU register map:
;   R1 = current write pointer
;   R2 = buffer start ($0A00)
;   R3 = buffer end+1 ($1000) - R1<R3 bounds check
;   R4 = scratch (view / scan / display iterator)
;   R5 = buffer last byte ($0FFF) - FILLMEMXY upper end for ^U
;
; Label map: 01=main loop  10/11/12=view  20/22=BS  30=delete
;            40/41=CR  50=clear  60/61/62/63/64=load-to-end  FE=exit

D 4000 CD 11 01 0A 00 11 02 0A 00 11 03 10 00 11 05 0F
D 4010 FF 10 00 00 B3 01 CB 81 00 18 A2 FE 81 00 16 A2
D 4020 10 81 00 08 A2 20 81 00 04 A2 30 81 00 0D A2 40
D 4030 81 00 15 A2 50 81 00 05 A2 60 89 13 A3 01 C9 36
D 4040 01 01 42 01 B4 01 B3 10 CA 0D CA 0A 23 00 24 B3
D 4050 11 87 14 A2 12 35 01 04 C9 42 04 B4 11 B3 12 CA
D 4060 0D CA 0A B4 01 B3 20 88 12 A3 01 43 01 35 01 01
D 4070 81 00 0A A3 22 88 12 A3 22 43 01 B3 22 CA 08 CA
D 4080 20 CA 08 B4 01 B3 30 88 12 A3 01 43 01 35 01 01
D 4090 81 00 0A A3 01 88 12 A3 01 43 01 B4 01 B3 40 89
D 40A0 13 A3 41 36 01 01 42 01 89 13 A3 41 10 00 0A 36
D 40B0 01 01 42 01 B3 41 CA 0D CA 0A B4 01 B3 FE 10 00
D 40C0 00 36 01 01 CA 0D CA 0A 00 B3 50 FB 25 00 23 00
D 40D0 21 CA 0D CA 0A B4 01 B3 60 23 00 24 B3 61 87 43
D 40E0 A2 62 35 01 04 81 00 00 A2 62 42 04 B4 61 B3 62
D 40F0 23 00 41 CA 0D CA 0A 23 00 24 B3 63 87 14 A2 64
D 4100 35 01 04 C9 42 04 B4 63 B3 64 B4 01

; ---- pre-pass END MARKER (added 2026-07-07) ----
;   Code ends at $410B (B4 01). Without F0 00 00 the label pre-pass
;   scans dirty RAM past here and can corrupt the 16 labels / 30
;   branches (the Prime-Gen bug class). Marker stops the scan cleanly.
D 410C F0 00 00
D 5000 00
D 6000 00
D 7000 00
